Please refer to https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-help/2005-February/066041.html
主要的原因, 從 help file (看help file 指令: ? fisher.test) 來看:

      Note this fails (with an error message) when the entries of the table
      are too large.

Note, the _entries_, not the dimensions.  The issue is how many tables
need to be enumerated.

Brian D. Ripley 的建議是你應該用 log-linear model 來了解資料間的dependence, 然後可以藉此更了解你的data.

For anyone wants to reproduce the result:
table <- matrix(c(32, 153, 167, 86, 3, 5234, 13017, 4088, 883, 225, 3, 8, 1, 2, 1), 3, 5, dimnames= list(B13 = c(1:3), B14 = c(1:5)))
fisher.test(table)

如果只是想讓他動:
fisher.test(a, simulate.p.value = TRUE, B = 20000)

